course: dictionary
lesson: 1759
title: Cleanly: neat and smooth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cleanly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. It usually means in a neat, smooth way, with one quick, even cut or break and no mess. Look at the words around it to find the meaning.
explain: «A hydrogen vehicle mixes hydrogen with oxygen from the air in a fuel cell to make electricity, and the only thing from its exhaust is water; hydrogen is still hard to make cleanly and has few filling stations.» Here cleanly means without making things dirty. Try the swap: "hard to make without making things dirty" still makes sense.
explain: In craft, a sharp knife cuts cleanly. In science, a stick can break cleanly. In sport, a goalkeeper catches the ball cleanly. «Tempering» chocolate makes it «snap cleanly». Each time, the clue is the same: no mess, no ragged edges, no fumble.
fact: Cleanly means in a neat, smooth way, with one quick, even cut or break and no mess.
fact: Cleanly can also mean in a way that does not make things dirty, such as burning cleanly.
fact: In sport, cleanly means fairly and well, without a foul or a fumble.
fact: Useful phrases: cut cleanly, break cleanly, burn cleanly, catch cleanly.
fact: «Snap cleanly» means breaking into two neat pieces with no mess.
exercise: «The sharp knife cut the card cleanly.» What does cleanly mean here? | *In a neat, smooth way with no mess | Carelessly, with ragged edges | Slowly and with a lot of noise | Very quickly and angrily
exercise: «The goalkeeper caught the ball cleanly.» In sport, what does cleanly suggest? | Threw it at the referee | *Caught it fairly and well, without a fumble | Dropped it on the grass | Kicked it hard into the net
exercise: Which phrase uses cleanly to mean without making things dirty? | sleep cleanly | *burn cleanly | cry cleanly | shout cleanly
test: «The chocolate snapped cleanly into two neat pieces.» What does cleanly mean here? | Into many crumbs | Loudly, with a crack like thunder | *In a neat way with no mess or ragged edges | Slowly and sadly
test: Nadia says cleanly is just another word for clean. Why is she only half right? | Cleanly means dirty | Cleanly is always a noun for a shiny thing | They mean exactly the same thing in every sentence | *Cleanly describes how something is done, like cutting neatly, while clean is more often about having no dirt
exam: Jayden reads «The fuel cell burns cleanly, and its only exhaust is water.» What does burns cleanly suggest? | It burns and then breaks into pieces | It burns very slowly and loudly | *It burns without making dirty waste | It burns only in the dark
